{
  "facts": [
    "The requested migration targets macOS and Linux judging hosts. Windows compatibility is outside the requested scope; do not add Windows-specific code. Existing untouched Windows branches in core helpers do not expand this migration requirement.",
    "This library is not an OS sandbox. The judge deployment runs the entire harness and learner program as the same request sandbox user; server credentials remain in the privileged server process. Callers supply process isolation for untrusted programs. Preventing learners from reading model answers or their own request files is outside the security policy; do not add a harness/submission privilege split or symlink containment between them. Serving links does not grant filesystem permissions beyond the caller's OS user. Temporary asset assembly must nevertheless leave source files and linked directories unchanged.",
    "The HTML comparison preset retains the existing course harness contract: pixel equality of deterministic pages. It disables CSS animations and transitions and waits for fonts, but does not freeze JavaScript timers, randomness, or animated image frames. Dynamic exercises must use custom browser checks.",
    "HTML served-directory assembly treats source files and symlinks as complete overrides; a directory symlink overrides its whole subtree. Only actual source directories are merged into temporary directories, so shared assets never get written into linked source targets.",
    "Isolated judging copies only the problem directory. Ancestor asset lookup serves model-answer and submission subdirectories within it; shared course-level assets must be included inside each problem that requires them.",
    "Process termination cleanup is owned by the host: it provides and removes a per-run TMPDIR. Isolated CLI checks establish TMPDIR under their parent-owned temporary root; Judge supplies its own request scratch directory. Browser directory helpers provide normal async disposal and leave signal handling to the host, including graceful asynchronous shutdown. Direct library callers must own cleanup when disposal is interrupted.",
  ],
}
